    "evidence_text": "Tumor-specific Th17-polarized cells eradicate large established melanoma.\n\nResponse to self antigen imprints regulatory memory in tissues\n\nIn fact, these diseases often spontaneously resolve, despite persistent tissue autoantigen expression.\n\nThus, Treg cells function to confer \u2018regulatory memory\u2019 to the target tissue.\n\nDifferentiation of effector CD4 T cell populations (*).\n\nThey are also involved in autoimmunity, asthma, and allergic responses as well as in tumor immunity.\n\nMemory CD4+ T cells induce innate responses independently of pathogen\n\nInflammation induced by recognition of pathogen-associated molecular patterns markedly affects subsequent adaptive responses.\n\nWe asked whether the adaptive immune system can also affect the character and magnitude of innate inflammatory responses.\n\nAutoimmune T cell responses in the central nervous system\n\nInnate lymphoid cells: emerging insights in development, lineage relationships, and function.\n\nThe role of immune responses in tumor development is a central issue for tumor biology and immunology.\n\nIL-17 is an important cytokine for inflammatory and autoimmune diseases.\n\nIn contrast, administration of IL-17 inhibited CD8 T cell infiltration and increased MDSCs in tumors.\n\nFurthermore, the bacterial load was enhanced in IL-17-defective mice.",
